// The selection band, and what it picks.
//
// Left-dragging in the scene view draws a rectangle and, when the button comes
// up, selects every entity whose sprite lands inside it. Selection lives in the
// entity record itself (slot 23, bit 0) rather than in a list the editor keeps,
// which is what lets the scene view outline what is selected and the inspector
// list it without either of them owning the answer.
//
// A band that is a single pixel is a *click*, and a click that hit nothing clears
// the selection -- the behaviour every tool has, and the one that makes an
// accidental drag recoverable.

ed_band_take(int k) {
  if (k = 3) {
    ed_pick(0, ed_bx0(), ed_by0(), 0);
  }
} return void;

// The band, normalised so that dragging up-left and dragging down-right give the
// same rectangle. Four functions rather than one that answers a record, because
// each is one expression and a record would have to be allocated or owned.
ed_bx0() {
} return int fx_min((import ed_st)[13], inp_mx());

ed_bx1() {
} return int fx_max((import ed_st)[13], inp_mx());
